WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.269 --> 00:00:03.570
Why does Doflamingo wear Glasses?

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:05.540
Does he have sensitive eyes?

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:07.910
Maybe a bolt fashion statement?

00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:13.190
Or is there some other meaning behind them,
that connect to his complex character on a

00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:16.049
much deeper level than you might have thought.

00:00:16.049 --> 00:00:22.660
In this video we will explore who Doflamingo
truly is as at heart, what his conflict with

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:28.789
Luffy meant for the story and what makes him
one of the most iconic antagonists in the

00:00:28.789 --> 00:00:30.039
entire series.

00:00:30.039 --> 00:00:35.691
Oh yeah and before we get into it, if you
haven’t subscribed to the channel yet, make

00:00:35.691 --> 00:00:45.710
sure to hit that big red button below this
video.

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:51.180
Doflamingo is a special antagonist in the
story for a number of reasons.

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:56.700
His unusually early introduction into the
story, the fantastic and clever ways he uses

00:00:56.700 --> 00:01:03.120
his devil fruit, his conquerors Haki as well
as his eccentric appearance are just the tip

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:05.089
of the ice berg here.

00:01:05.089 --> 00:01:17.429
Because I believe that he is actually the
most complex villain in the story so far.

00:01:17.429 --> 00:01:23.290
Doflamingo is a former celestial Dragon, who
has been locked out of paradise.

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:28.759
Giving him this sort of backstory was a fantastic
move by Oda, as it ties his chaotic and evil

00:01:28.759 --> 00:01:34.340
nature together with one of THE major antagonistic
forces of the story.

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:38.539
Doflamingo is not just evil for evil’s sake.

00:01:38.539 --> 00:01:44.360
He is the tragic result of the unjust world
order, created by those around him.

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:50.679
His entire childhood, Doflamingo grew up under
the ideology that as a world noble he was

00:01:50.679 --> 00:01:52.999
practically a god.

00:01:52.999 --> 00:01:58.399
Having people serve at his will and ruling
over them with absolute control and power

00:01:58.399 --> 00:02:04.520
was not only an idea, but something that constituted
everyday life in Marijoe.

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:10.110
And yet, when his father decided to leave
this world of perverted excess, egotism and

00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:16.180
exploitation behind, he was suddenly confronted
with the harsh reality of the real world,

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:27.090
where there were no slaves to do the work
and satisfy his every desire.

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:33.350
In fact is was the exact opposite: Hated for
their heritage, his family was prosecuted

00:02:33.350 --> 00:02:34.920
by the commoners.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:39.850
Being forced to go into hiding and live off
garbage, eventually his mother succumbed to

00:02:39.850 --> 00:02:41.040
illness.

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:46.890
Finally, one day together with his father
Homing and his brother Corazon he was lynched

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:55.460
by an angry mob of commoners that had suffered
under the hand of

00:02:55.460 --> 00:02:57.840
the Tenryuubito.

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:04.100
This sudden transition from one extreme into
the other traumatised and broke the young

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:10.270
boy, who until then had known nothing but
pleasure and entitlement his entire life.

00:03:10.270 --> 00:03:21.570
And interestingly, while this tragic experience
brought out the very best in his brother Corazon

00:03:21.570 --> 00:03:25.880
it brought out the very worst in himself.

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:36.200
A wonderful example of nature vs nurture,
I think.

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:42.030
Maybe, in the end, the decisive factor between
the two brothers contrasting development was

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:47.819
that Rosinante was able to show and share
his emotions and pain, lauding, crying and

00:03:47.819 --> 00:03:51.010
suffering side by side with his parents.

00:03:51.010 --> 00:03:56.370
Doflamingo meanwhile could never show his
true feelings or connect to them on a human

00:03:56.370 --> 00:04:02.740
level and thus ended up projecting all of
his hate, fear and pain on his family.

00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:07.860
Being thrown into misery through the well-meaning,
but terribly naive decision of his father

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:13.990
to try and live a normal life, he felt betrayed,
ultimately covering his deep emotional wounds

00:04:13.990 --> 00:04:19.579
and sudden lack of self-confidence with rage
and the sense of importance he had been spoon

00:04:19.579 --> 00:04:21.280
fed his entire life.

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:26.759
Finally, when his traumatising experience
with the villagers was added to this already

00:04:26.759 --> 00:04:30.659
toxic brew of emotions, Doflamingo cracked.

00:04:30.659 --> 00:04:36.139
And I believe that it was at this point that
he truly gave in to ‘evil’ and as a result

00:04:36.139 --> 00:04:38.460
executes his father.

00:04:38.460 --> 00:05:02.410
This tragic past results in one of my absolute
favourite speeches of the show.

00:05:02.410 --> 00:05:07.909
As chance would have it, in this moment of
deepest darkness, he was discovered by none

00:05:07.909 --> 00:05:13.090
other than Trebol, who instead of showing
him care and love, once again hailed him as

00:05:13.090 --> 00:05:16.939
a king and as superior to all others.

00:05:16.939 --> 00:05:22.740
Filling the hole in his chest with even more
ideas of power and importance and being handed

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:28.439
the tools to act on them, Dofi started to
develop into the cruel and manipulative villain

00:05:28.439 --> 00:05:37.689
that Luffy encounters on Dressrosa.

00:05:37.689 --> 00:05:43.699
Betrayed from all sides - by his family, by
the nobles and by the people - he had seen

00:05:43.699 --> 00:05:50.690
just how cruel this world was and realised
that it needed to be reborn, in his message

00:05:50.690 --> 00:05:52.909
that is.

00:05:52.909 --> 00:05:58.000
However his lack of self-confidence and true
love would never allow for that.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:03.389
And so, while he loves nothing more than present
himself as a messenger of chaos and destruction,

00:06:03.389 --> 00:06:11.990
to the world at large, in reality we find
out that he is a control freak in every sense

00:06:11.990 --> 00:06:24.059
of the word, desperate to literally try and
pull all the strings behind the scene.

00:06:24.059 --> 00:06:29.479
He needs to be the puppeteer that has full
power over whatever is going on in his small

00:06:29.479 --> 00:06:30.479
world.

00:06:30.479 --> 00:06:36.120
And this is exactly the reason why betrayal
and disloyalty is the worst possible thing

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:53.159
for him as we see with Corazo - - 
and Law

00:06:53.159 --> 00:06:58.630
All of this also shows really well in the
relationship he has with his family.

00:06:58.630 --> 00:07:04.870
While, like a real Don, family seems to be
incredibly important to him, his relationship

00:07:04.870 --> 00:07:07.900
to his crew is quite screwed.

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:12.669
There is no doubt that he does seem to care
for them to a certain extend, as we can see

00:07:12.669 --> 00:07:20.210
after Vergo’s and Monet’s death or the
lengths he went to to protect baby five.

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:30.809
However, the things that matter most to him
are absolute loyalty and dedication.

00:07:30.809 --> 00:07:36.110
While it might pain him to sacrifice one of
his family members, he will do so to reach

00:07:36.110 --> 00:07:37.440
his goal.

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:43.059
After all, he is a king, a god, who stands
above everyone else.

00:07:43.059 --> 00:07:52.229
His will has priority.

00:07:52.229 --> 00:07:57.839
In many ways Luffy and Doflamingo are two
sides of the same coin.

00:07:57.839 --> 00:08:03.409
Just like Dofi, Luffy also strongly values
the wild patchwork family he has gathered

00:08:03.409 --> 00:08:06.860
around him and those close to him.

00:08:06.860 --> 00:08:12.120
However never in his wildest dreams would
Luffy put his own ambition over that of his

00:08:12.120 --> 00:08:18.339
crew, nor sacrifice even a single one of them
for any of his goals.

00:08:18.339 --> 00:08:23.659
Because the straw hats, other than the Donquixote
pirates are a crucial part of his ambitions

00:08:23.659 --> 00:08:27.530
to begin with, and not just pawns to be used.

00:08:27.530 --> 00:08:32.840
It is one of THE major underlaying messages
of the story: It doesn’t really matter what

00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:44.270
type of values you hold, but how you act on
them in the world.

00:08:44.270 --> 00:08:49.620
. Dofi feels like he is entitled to be king
and stand above everyone else, he is just

00:08:49.620 --> 00:08:55.240
taking what is rightfully his through pure
strength and power of will.

00:08:55.240 --> 00:09:01.091
Luffy meanwhile, also is convinced he can
become king and takes what he wants, and he

00:09:01.091 --> 00:09:04.320
does so by pure strength and willpower as
well.

00:09:04.320 --> 00:09:11.310
However, where they fundamentally differ from
each other is in their incentive: Dofi wants

00:09:11.310 --> 00:09:16.810
to rule and control others and fill the hole
in his heart by seeking the ultimate form

00:09:16.810 --> 00:09:18.470
of attention.

00:09:18.470 --> 00:09:24.100
Luffy on the other hand, simply wants to be
free.

00:09:24.100 --> 00:09:34.450
Doflamingo’s Nakama serve him, while Luffy’s
crew are his equals, each with dreams and

00:09:34.450 --> 00:09:36.490
ambitions of their own.

00:09:36.490 --> 00:09:41.210
Dofi has subordinates and business partners
that want a piece of the cake, while Luffy

00:09:41.210 --> 00:09:46.660
has friends and allies and people that trust
and believe in him and genuinely want him

00:09:46.660 --> 00:09:48.970
to succeed and be happy.

00:09:48.970 --> 00:09:53.940
They give Luffy purpose and together guide
him towards the right path.

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:59.370
Helping and fighting for his friends is what
got Luffy this far in the first place.

00:09:59.370 --> 00:10:02.810
At first it was Shanks who inspired his dream.

00:10:02.810 --> 00:10:07.550
Then it was the love and pain he shared with
his brothers that made him fight for his dream

00:10:07.550 --> 00:10:09.120
in earnest.

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:14.950
And finally, it was his crew that helps him
do the impossible and defy the world to reach

00:10:14.950 --> 00:10:17.240
their dreams together.

00:10:17.240 --> 00:10:21.500
All of them believing in him, but none of
them going easy on him.

00:10:21.500 --> 00:10:23.640
Dofi never had that.

00:10:23.640 --> 00:10:29.600
Corrupted by the perverse ideology of the
nobles and maybe also cursed by his nature,

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:34.710
he never had the capability of laughing and
crying with his family.

00:10:34.710 --> 00:10:40.660
As for his executives, they never gave him
anything to fight and strive for, they just

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:45.660
told him that he was entitled to be king and
rule over all anyway.

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:52.910
As they like to say, it is very lonely, alone
at the top.

00:10:52.910 --> 00:11:00.600
This pattern just keeps going the deeper you
dig.

00:11:00.600 --> 00:11:06.220
Dofi despises the Tenryuubito and wants to
tear down the old world for all the injustice

00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:08.800
and pain it has inflicted on him.

00:11:08.800 --> 00:11:13.240
Luffy also despises the Nobles and the world
government, however because of what they have

00:11:13.240 --> 00:11:15.630
done to his friends, not to him.

00:11:15.630 --> 00:11:21.920
And while Dofi envisions a new world, where
only the strong will make the cut, ironically

00:11:21.920 --> 00:11:26.750
he is the only holding the old world together
by pulling the stings from the underworld,

00:11:26.750 --> 00:11:38.180
working with both the World Government and
the Yonko to secure his position.

00:11:38.180 --> 00:11:43.290
Only through his defeat by Luffy is the world
thrown into real chaos as Dofi is the very

00:11:43.290 --> 00:11:47.680
first to not make the cut for this new world
order.

00:11:47.680 --> 00:11:53.680
This deep irony makes him one of the most
tragic characters in the story, I believe.

00:11:53.680 --> 00:11:59.370
And so, this brings me to the main point of
this video, that I think many people overlook

00:11:59.370 --> 00:12:04.710
when it comes to Doflamingo’s character.

00:12:04.710 --> 00:12:13.790
You see, based on all that we have discussed
so far, I believe that the biggest irony of

00:12:13.790 --> 00:12:19.580
the entire Dressrosa arc was the Bird cage
and all the other bird symbolism united in

00:12:19.580 --> 00:12:24.300
a man that Oda literally named Doflamingo.

00:12:24.300 --> 00:12:29.350
Because he is literally a fragile and exotic
bird that is caged himself.

00:12:29.350 --> 00:12:31.610
Let me explain.

00:12:31.610 --> 00:12:36.830
In many ways Doflamingo has always been the
puppet of others, never really having any

00:12:36.830 --> 00:12:41.680
say or control of his own life, his dreams
or his destiny.

00:12:41.680 --> 00:12:47.050
The tragedy however was that he never saw
the strings himself.

00:12:47.050 --> 00:12:52.770
He never really heard the commands to follow
his purpose, never saw the walls raised around

00:12:52.770 --> 00:12:58.530
him - isolating him from the world, never
felt the push of other people using him for

00:12:58.530 --> 00:13:03.270
their own interests, but he always followed
through on them.

00:13:03.270 --> 00:13:06.890
The Celestial Dragons told him to behave like
a god.

00:13:06.890 --> 00:13:11.220
His father made him atone for his own bad
conscience and experience hell.

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:15.700
Then the world nobles treated him like an
outcast, pushing him away.

00:13:15.700 --> 00:13:21.690
Trebol and the other executives told him to
behave like a king and strive for power.

00:13:21.690 --> 00:13:26.950
And finally he was working for the government
and Kaido, keeping control over his small

00:13:26.950 --> 00:13:32.110
island, where he would be able to tyrannise
the people and play god, while working for

00:13:32.110 --> 00:13:35.200
other people’s dreams and ambitions.

00:13:35.200 --> 00:13:41.570
Not once in his entire life did Dofi have
the chance to learn who he truly is and what

00:13:41.570 --> 00:13:47.180
he wants in life, always a slave to the ideals
of others.

00:13:47.180 --> 00:13:53.790
This is why Luffy will be the king of pirates,
and Dofi never had a chance to play the game

00:13:53.790 --> 00:13:55.890
in the first place.

00:13:55.890 --> 00:14:10.420
Because to become pirate king and change the
world, you need one thing above all: Freedom.

00:14:10.420 --> 00:14:16.380
And so, once again it took Luffy to literally
break the bird cage that held this rare and

00:14:16.380 --> 00:14:22.180
exotic Flamingo his entire life by shattering
all the expectations and stories about being

00:14:22.180 --> 00:14:28.410
special that he had been fed his entire life
and that had dictated his every move.

00:14:28.410 --> 00:14:32.620
He wanted to be the puppet master, but ended
up being the puppet.

00:14:32.620 --> 00:14:38.350
He was supposed to be a bird that could fly
free, but in the end was locked in a cage

00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:41.080
his entire life.

00:14:41.080 --> 00:14:48.010
This is why in his battle with Luffy, Dofi
is a man with no love, no freedom and no dream

00:14:48.010 --> 00:14:54.710
of his own and as a result has nothing left
to lose: And so, by completely destroying

00:14:54.710 --> 00:15:01.860
him and everything he worked for, as he so
often does, Luffy not only frees dressrosa,

00:15:01.860 --> 00:15:04.350
but Doflamingo as well.

00:15:04.350 --> 00:15:11.370
The moment his cage crumbles and falls, Dofi
finally escapes the prison he built himself

00:15:11.370 --> 00:15:13.010
unknowingly.

00:15:13.010 --> 00:15:17.530
And so, while we don’t know the original
reason that Doflamingo started wearing glasses

00:15:17.530 --> 00:15:23.430
in the first place, the fact that he was wearing
shades his entire life, really symbolises

00:15:23.430 --> 00:15:27.550
well the shadow under which he has lived since
his childhood.

00:15:27.550 --> 00:15:33.860
And Luffy finally breaking these glasses as
he beats Dofi into the ground, finally gives

00:15:33.860 --> 00:15:36.070
him a glimpse into the light.

00:15:36.070 --> 00:15:44.430
The only question that remains is whether
he will actually notice.

00:15:44.430 --> 00:15:54.040
I think what Doflamingo’s character really
is supposed to show us, is just how cruel,

00:15:54.040 --> 00:15:59.820
toxic and unjust the world is under the rule
of the Tenryuubito and how the system that

00:15:59.820 --> 00:16:04.760
the world government has created produces
true despair and evil.

00:16:04.760 --> 00:16:10.940
And so Doflamingo and the entire Dressrosa
arc ultimately present to us the true nature

00:16:10.940 --> 00:16:13.110
of the world in miniature.

00:16:13.110 --> 00:16:20.070
In the end Doflamingo is just another tragic
victim of this system and Luffy is once again

00:16:20.070 --> 00:16:23.130
the one that works to abolish it.

00:16:23.130 --> 00:16:28.740
And so I believe that it’s all of these
complex layers that are woven into Doflamingo’s

00:16:28.740 --> 00:16:41.820
character, that make him one the most interesting
&amp; fascinating villains in anime.

00:16:41.820 --> 00:16:47.170
There is another aspect to Doflamingo’s
character, that I found incredibly interesting,

00:16:47.170 --> 00:16:50.920
that however didn’t really fit into the
context of this video.

00:16:50.920 --> 00:16:53.870
The similarities between him and Crocodile.

00:16:53.870 --> 00:16:59.060
So, I decided to make a small bonus video
on the topic, that you can watch on the left.

00:16:59.060 --> 00:17:04.589
Or, if you already want to look at the next
villain in the story, you can learn how Katakuri

00:17:04.589 --> 00:17:08.150
was able to win the fight against Luffy on
the right.

00:17:08.150 --> 00:17:09.150
Thanks guys.

00:17:09.150 --> 00:17:09.839
Peace.

